@@s041 <code>ReentrantLock</code>
@@s042 the smallest possible critical section
@@s043 extra lines inside the lock
@@s044 <code>ReentrantLock</code> to print <code>-|-|-|…</code>
@@s045 <code>ReentrantLock</code> + check before the increment (exactly 15000)
@@s046 intrinsic locks (<code>synchronized</code>) for the readers-writers monitor
@@s047 2.1.5 (challenging)
@@s048 <code>ReentrantLock</code> with <b>two</b> condition variables (readers and writers), signal only when needed
@@s049 <code>synchronized</code> on the methods of <code>MutableInteger</code>
@@s050 <code>volatile</code> on <code>value</code>
@@s051 all the locks (they must be removed)
@@s052 a new <code>Mystery</code> without race condition
@@s053 do not change the modifiers: no static ↔ instance on fields or methods
@@s054 only <code>Semaphore</code>; FIFO queue with <b>non</b>-thread-safe collections that implement <code>Queue</code> (e.g. <code>LinkedList</code>) or arrays; constructor with the size; state the concrete exception
@@s055 <code>Lock</code>, <code>synchronized</code>, any concurrent collection (<code>BlockingQueue</code>…)
@@s056 intrinsic locks (<code>synchronized</code>); you can add attributes, even <code>static</code>
@@s057 4.3.1 (challenging)
@@s058 a semaphore built with <code>Lock</code>
@@s059 <code>java.util.concurrent.Semaphore</code>
@@s060 4.3.2 (challenging)
@@s061 a non-cyclic barrier built with <b>your</b> semaphore from 4.3.1
