@@s063 The table grows with the new exercise sheets: every week I add the new constraints.
@@s064 Mistakes that cost the approval
@@s065 Vague explanation
@@s066 "The lock avoids the problems". It is missing what the critical section is, why two threads cannot be there together, which interleavings are excluded.
@@s067 Proof by execution
@@s068 "I ran it and it always prints 20 million". A test does not prove the absence of errors: reasoning is needed.
@@s069 Terms swapped
@@s070 data race ≠ race condition; synchronization action ≠ variable access; program order ≠ happens-before between threads.
@@s071 Missing part
@@s072 A mandatory exercise not done = assignment not approved, even if the rest is perfect.
